wxChaos Changelog
------------------
- Version 2.0.0
    - Major rewrite of the codebase.
    - Complete redesign of the user interface.
    - Added a dark theme.
    - Standardized rendering algorithms, allowing most fractals to share the same rendering algorithms.
    - Added dedicated documentation for each fractal.
    - Added viewport manipulation tools.
    - Added smooth zooming.
    - Added a settings menu.
    - Added support for user-defined Newton–Raphson formulas.
    - Improved zoom recorder precision.
    - Improved the command console with better syntax handling, autocompletion, and command history.
    - Improved multithreading performance.
    - Added new color palettes and color-mapping options.
    - Added multiprecision rendering, allowing users to perform arbitrarily deep zooms.
    - Added perturbation rendering for Mandelbrot and Julia sets, significantly improving deep-zoom performance.
    - Added supersampling anti-aliasing.
    - Fixed various crashes and stability issues.

- Version 1.1.0
	- Linux: Modified the installing directories according to the Ubuntu store guidelines.

- Version 1.0.3
	- Switched to the double precision model on the scripting language.
	- Script fractals now plot on "x" and "y" instead of "real" and "imaginary".
	- Added cut billiard fractal.
	- Fixed a linking problem on Ubuntu 13.04

- Version 1.0.2
	- Fixed a bug on the WASD navigation.

- Version 1.0.1
	- Added support for unicode build.
	- Parser now reports errors.
	- Fixed bug that made Julia Mode crash.
	- "AddLine" command added.
	- Fixed Show Orbit bug that made some lines to be rendered incorrectly.
	- Various bugfixes.
	- Linux support.
